🧠 Introduction

Training AI models from scratch is expensive and time-consuming.

👉 **Transfer Learning** solves this problem by reusing knowledge from pre-trained models.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is Transfer Learning?

```text
Using a pre-trained model and adapting it to a new task
```

---

🎯 Why Transfer Learning?

✔ Saves time
✔ Requires less data
✔ Improves performance
✔ Reduces computational cost

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧩 How Transfer Learning Works

1️⃣ Train model on large dataset (pretraining)
2️⃣ Reuse model for new task
3️⃣ Fine-tune on smaller dataset

---

🔁 Workflow

```text id="n8x4qp"
Pretrained Model → Fine-Tuning → Task-Specific Model
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🤖 Transfer Learning in Hugging Face

Hugging Face makes transfer learning easy using:

* Transformers
* Pre-trained models
* Trainer API

---

⚙️ Installation

```bash id="z7m2pl"
pip install transformers datasets
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📥 Load Pre-trained Model

```python id="r4k8qn"
from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSequenceClassification

model_name = "bert-base-uncased"

tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)
model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(model_name)
```

---

🔹 Tokenization

```python id="x5p2mv"
text = "I love AI"

inputs = tokenizer(text, return_tensors="pt")
```

---

🔹 Fine-Tuning (Concept)

```text id="q1m7zp"
Train model on your custom dataset
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

💻 Example: Simple Fine-Tuning Setup

```python id="k6x9dp"
from transformers import Trainer, TrainingArguments

training_args = TrainingArguments(
    output_dir="./results",
    num_train_epochs=1,
    per_device_train_batch_size=8
)

trainer = Trainer(
    model=model,
    args=training_args,
    train_dataset=None  # Replace with your dataset
)
```

